      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/21/virginia-child-dies-measles",
      "description": "<p>Death adds to national measles outbreak that recently cost the US its measles elimination status after 26 years</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia\">Virginia</a> reported its first measles-associated death of 2026 ⁠on Friday, involving a child who tested positive for the infectious disease, the state’s health department said.</p><p>The department said the child was ⁠age four or younger. It did not disclose additional details, including the child’s vaccination status, citing the family’s privacy.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/21/virginia-child-dies-measles\">Continue reading...</a>",
